    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d753">

                <pb facs="0717" n="705" sameAs="frus:frus1940v01/pg705"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862.857/85: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Panama</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Dawson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Panama</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-03-06T10:00:00-05:00">March 6, 1940—10
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 12:35 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>29. Department’s telegram No. 25 of March 2, 4 p.m.<anchor n="33"
                        xml:id="d753-f1"/> The proposed text is acceptable to the Panamanian
                    Government.</p>
                <p>In the second paragraph of its telegram the Department states that the note is to
                    be delivered to the British Government by the President of Panama. Doctor Garay
                    points out that the President would address any communication to the King of
                    England and that as drafted the Brazilian text seems to contemplate a note to be
                    addressed by the Panamanian Foreign Office to the British Government through the
                    British Minister in Panama. Further advices from the Department as to the
                    procedure desired in this respect would be appreciated. In <pb facs="0718"
                        n="706" xml:id="pg706"/> the case of the <hi rendition="#italic">Graf
                        Spee</hi> incident the protest was addressed by the President of Panama to
                    the several chiefs of state.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>[<hi rendition="#small-caps">Dawson</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
